Archive protocol timestamps and hashes, exact source and diffs, all benchmark blobs/recipes, compiler flags, interpreter/dependency versions, machine metadata, source signatures and decisions, exact ANF digests, independent correctness results, all raw timing/memory/operation rows, failures/timeouts, profile scope, analysis code, and final tables. Preserve old records and corrections side by side.

## Decision after this experiment

If exact Python dispatch remains slow but clean always-folded lowering has substantial savings on held-out opportunities, a compiled observer/common-factory experiment is justified. If a better direct kernel removes most practical benefit, prioritize shared ANF algorithms or narrow the workload claim. If natural opportunities are too rare, publish the mechanism and measured applicability boundary instead of a general compiler speedup.

For native work, freeze a factorial with a shared compiled source factory and shared ANF core wherever compiled. Compare direct telemetry-off, telemetry-on forced bypass, selected folding, and generic folding. Share node allocation, interning, canonicalization, ownership, integer widths/overflow guards, API crossings, memoization, kernel, instrumentation, and validation placement. Report incremental metadata cost, FFI/cold startup, lower-only and total timings. A telemetry-only native helper can be evaluated separately as an implementation intervention; it does not substitute for matched native-direct versus native-folded evidence.
